          "name": "Grafana Search Playlists",
          "request": {
            "name": "Grafana Search Playlists",
            "description": {
              "content": "The GET /playlists endpoint in Grafana allows users to retrieve a list of playlists based on search criteria. This operation queries the Grafana instance for playlists that match specified parameters, returning playlist metadata such as name, ID, and associated dashboards. Users can filter results using query parameters to narrow down playlists by name or other attributes. The endpoint returns a JSON array containing the matching playlists, making it useful for administrators and users who need to discover, list, or programmatically access available playlists within their Grafana environment. This is particularly valuable in environments with multiple playlists where users need to search and identify specific playlist configurations without manually browsing through the Grafana interface.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
